WEBVTT

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:50.700
You'll definitely remember, Kaito!

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:03.180
Seira!

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:12.300
Seira, I'll definitely get your orange heart shards back!

00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:16.150
The Last Love Letter

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:22.070
Wow, this tent is huge! I never knew they could be so roomy.

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:23.240
{Isn't that so}Isn't it, Hanon?

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:26.790
I always wanted to go camping sometime.

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:28.860
When you go to sleep, you use a sleeping bag.

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:30.950
Really? It sounds like fun.

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:36.460
It's so spacious that I can spread myself out.

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:40.930
Of course it is. This tent is for six people.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:44.270
Then, when Lucia and Rina come here, they'd be able to join us.

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:47.720
Yeah. It'd be fine if they brought along their boyfriends, too.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:49.150
Boyfriends?

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:52.160
You wouldn't mind if we were a couple, would you?

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:55.680
Goodness! What are you rambling about, Nagisa?

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:57.520
Excuse me, you two...

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:02.670
I'm sorry, but I'm afraid this tent is for display and not for resting.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:06.350
Isn't it about time to come out of there?

00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:08.700
Yes. We're sorry.

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:10.350
Excuse us!

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:15.000
Geez! Nagisa, you shouldn't have suggested to come to that outdoor store.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:17.880
I was embarrassed.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:21.180
Wasn't it you who was laid out in the tent?

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.780
You did as well!

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:26.380
Anyway, let's go camping someday.

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:27.710
Yeah, of course.

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:39.010
I'm back.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:42.970
Welcome back, Hanon. You've got a letter from Mitsuki-sensei!

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:44.830
What? From Tarou-chan?

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:49.170
Here. It's the first time Mitsuki-sensei wrote to you, isn't it?

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:50.450
How wonderful, Hanon!

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:52.180
Y-Yeah.

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:54.970
What's wrong, Hanon? Aren't you happy?

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:58.840
Eh!? N-Nagisa-kun...

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:04.250
H-Hanon, I'm sorry! I didn't... mean it...

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:06.370
Nagisa, thank you for taking me home.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:08.390
See you tomorrow at school.

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:11.120
Yeah. See you later, Hanon.

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:18.470
Hanon, I'm very sorry! I didn't know that Nagisa-kun came here with you.

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:21.200
No. It's all right.

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:23.290
Don't worry about it, Lucia.

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:46.950
Tarou-chan...

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:28.780
What happened to Hanon?

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:30.970
She's been distracted since this morning.

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:31.610
Yeah.

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:38.450
Maybe it's that I handed her the letter from Mitsuki-sensei in front of Nagisa-kun yesterday.

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:43.430
I don't think so. They've been getting along very well with each other.

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:45.420
Then why?

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:46.670
No idea.

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:52.540
But that letter must have been the cause of this.

00:06:53.020 --> 00:06:57.980
It probably reminds her of the memories she had with Mitsuki-sensei.

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:02.490
She must have been taken with Mitsuki-sensei then.

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:06.350
Ah, Nagisa-kun.

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:11.450
What are you doing!?

00:07:11.650 --> 00:07:12.550
Nagisa...?

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:16.120
Hey, that hurt! What was that for!?

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:19.460
Nothing, I was trying to cheer you up.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:25.080
Geez! Do you think a hard slap on the shoulder is the best way to cheer someone up?

00:07:25.230 --> 00:07:27.250
I just wanted to try to cheer you up.

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:30.590
Huh? What {did you say}are you saying? Are you stupid?

00:07:30.820 --> 00:07:33.300
{There,}See? You're back to {the way you always were.}your old self.

00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:36.590
{Then,}So do you have anything else to {tell}say to me?

00:07:36.790 --> 00:07:39.240
Hanon, {will}do you want to go for a {drive}ride with me?

00:07:39.340 --> 00:07:40.770
Huh? A ride?

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:43.990
Let's go for a ride with my wheels.{own vehicle!}

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:49.830
What? Your wheels? But you don't have a driver's license.

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:53.940
Anyway, I'll pick you up tomorrow. See you later.

00:07:54.630 --> 00:07:57.920
What is he {going to do?}planning?

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:09.560
Ahh! I can't write!

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:13.520
Come in.

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:18.060
Hanon! You didn't eat any dinner, and you shut yourself in your room.

00:08:18.110 --> 00:08:19.900
What are you doing?

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:24.520
Ah, you're writing a return letter to Mitsuki-sensei.

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:25.460
I guess so.

00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:27.860
You seem be struggling with writing that letter.

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:33.320
That's because I have no idea what to write.

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:38.300
I don't think you have to take it so seriously. Just write what you feel.

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:40.420
Lucia is right, Hanon.

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:46.000
You may be right. But I don't understand myself.

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:47.920
Hanon?

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:52.610
Why did I love Tarou-chan so much back then?

00:08:53.020 --> 00:08:55.650
Why do I find it enjoyable to be with Nagisa now?

00:08:56.320 --> 00:09:03.100
But ever since I got the letter from Tarou-chan, all I can think of is him.

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:06.320
Do you think I'm going crazy?

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:51.390
Love. It is the hope that allows the Mermaid Princesses to live on.

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:55.500
Love. It is the sustenance of the Mermaid Princesses that allows them to live.

00:09:55.750 --> 00:09:59.960
{From ancient times}From the beginning, love has been indispensable to the Mermaid Princesses.

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:02.720
So do you have a concrete battle plan?

00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:06.060
I'll use their tendency to gravitate towards love to lure them in.

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:09.280
Then I'll trap them by using love.

00:10:09.820 --> 00:10:14.030
Hehe! You are much more excited than usual, Lady Bat.

00:10:16.430 --> 00:10:22.190
This time, I'll show them an illusion from my brilliant ball of light.

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:33.580
Good morning, Hanon! Are you there?

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:35.870
What happened, Nagisa?

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:39.390
As we promised yesterday, let's go for a ride with my wheels.

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:42.000
What!? Were you really serious yesterday?

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:44.680
Why would I lie to you?

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:48.610
B-But, I thought that your idea of a "ride" was a joke.

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:50.700
Whatever! Let's go!

00:10:50.930 --> 00:10:52.310
W-Wait a minute!

00:10:56.240 --> 00:10:59.020
What do you think? Aren't my wheels cool?

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:01.570
It's just a bike...

00:11:01.700 --> 00:11:04.660
Yeah! It's a tandem. Isn't it great?

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:07.110
All right, Hanon. Let's go for a ride!

00:11:07.240 --> 00:11:08.590
We're going on this?

00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:23.930
Hey, Hanon. Why didn't you say that you couldn't ride a bike in the first place?

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:26.990
Because I didn't know that I couldn't until I got on it.

00:11:27.400 --> 00:11:29.640
It's easy for anyone to do!

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:33.290
You can say that, but this is the first time I got on one.

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:36.890
How in the world could you have lived without riding a bike?

00:11:37.100 --> 00:11:40.750
That's because there's no need to ride a bike in the sea.

00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:43.070
Huh? In the sea?

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:46.260
Anyway, I've never ridden a bike!

00:11:46.340 --> 00:11:49.700
Sometimes, I don't understand you, Hanon.

00:12:09.170 --> 00:12:13.000
Oww... I've got a cramp in my leg!

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:14.940
Are you okay, Nagisa?

00:12:15.020 --> 00:12:17.190
I'm all right. It's nothing.

00:12:17.930 --> 00:12:20.610
I'm sorry. It's all because I couldn't ride a bike.

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:22.780
Idiot. Quit moping like that.

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:23.720
Eh?

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:27.120
I wanted to have a fun time with you.

00:12:27.730 --> 00:12:30.460
It doesn't mean a thing if you look so sad.

00:12:31.760 --> 00:12:32.710
Nagisa.

00:12:47.070 --> 00:12:51.180
The biggest illusion show of this century: "The Lovers' Evening."

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:55.160
Many young lovers will gather to see this show.

00:12:55.730 --> 00:12:58.230
The Mermaid Princesses will show up, too.

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:02.230
Come, lovers! Show yourselves, Mermaid Princesses!

00:13:02.850 --> 00:13:05.680
Come to this place where the stars fall into the ocean!

00:13:08.280 --> 00:13:09.640
Who is that woman?

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:10.710
She's weird.

00:13:10.940 --> 00:13:12.490
I should tell my mom about her.

00:13:12.670 --> 00:13:14.050
Yeah, me too.

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:17.090
Hey, Nagisa. Where are we?

00:13:17.210 --> 00:13:19.360
Uh-oh. I think we're lost.

00:13:19.460 --> 00:13:20.230
Eh?

00:13:20.990 --> 00:13:24.110
From this address, it looks like we're still in the city.

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:26.990
But, I've never seen this scenery before.

00:13:27.350 --> 00:13:29.800
Oh well. Don't worry about it.

00:13:30.230 --> 00:13:34.620
When I was in elementary school, I used to ride to really far away places.

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:35.590
Really?

00:13:35.690 --> 00:13:38.750
Yeah. It was exciting when I rode into another town.

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:41.360
Oh, I think I get it!

00:13:41.360 --> 00:13:46.970
When I was little, it made my heart skip a beat when I swam into another kingdom.

00:13:47.020 --> 00:13:49.170
Huh? Another kingdom?

00:13:49.350 --> 00:13:51.740
Um, sorry. Never mind.

00:13:53.300 --> 00:13:54.910
It's called "The Lovers' Evening."

00:13:54.960 --> 00:13:56.030
Oh? That sounds like fun!

00:13:56.030 --> 00:13:56.640
What's that?

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:57.460
I don't know.

00:13:57.770 --> 00:14:00.010
It's the biggest illusion show of the century!

00:14:00.750 --> 00:14:02.310
Hanon, let's take a look.

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:02.770
Huh?

00:14:07.310 --> 00:14:08.950
It's so crowded.

00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:11.340
Most of them are couples.

00:14:11.520 --> 00:14:14.300
This is a "lovers' evening," isn't it?

00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:24.210
Ladies and gentlemen, and my dearest lovers.

00:14:24.490 --> 00:14:26.730
Welcome to my show.

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:30.460
Let me start my {illusion}illusory show of love.

00:14:58.480 --> 00:14:59.860
This song is...

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:22.040
Hanon, what's wrong? Are you okay?

00:15:22.190 --> 00:15:23.520
That light...

00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:24.510
That light?

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:28.240
That light seems to makes me feel uncomfortable.

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:38.500
Being bathed in that light should torture the Mermaid Princesses.

00:15:38.800 --> 00:15:39.980
Now, show yourselves!

00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:45.060
Hanon, pull yourself together!

00:15:45.390 --> 00:15:47.920
Hang in there! I'll help you somehow.

00:15:57.560 --> 00:16:00.040
Don't disturb my show!

00:16:01.190 --> 00:16:02.590
Nagisa!

00:16:06.550 --> 00:16:08.430
Aqua Pearl Voice!

00:16:15.250 --> 00:16:18.000
Welcome, Mermaid Princess.

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:22.160
The real illusion {that will}to make you suffer is {just beginning.}about to begin.

00:16:44.320 --> 00:16:46.510
No, I'm not going to lose! I can't lose!

00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:50.490
I {should}have to protect Nagisa, who protected me.

00:16:50.620 --> 00:16:53.730
But when I hear this song, I...

00:17:47.480 --> 00:17:49.220
Pink Pearl Voice!

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:53.430
Green Pearl Voice!

00:17:54.700 --> 00:17:56.260
Hanon, pull yourself together!

00:17:57.710 --> 00:17:59.480
Rina! Lucia!

00:17:59.730 --> 00:18:04.580
Now, Lady Bat! It's our turn to show the real illusion!

00:18:04.660 --> 00:18:05.780
Brace yourself!

00:18:07.590 --> 00:18:08.560
W-Wait a minute!

00:19:01.360 --> 00:19:03.840
All right, let's go!

00:19:04.300 --> 00:19:07.260
Pichi Pichi Voice Live Start!

00:19:36.940 --> 00:19:39.950
All three of you show up the moment I finish my song!

00:19:40.080 --> 00:19:42.060
No fair! That's not fair!

00:20:11.980 --> 00:20:15.220
I {see now}get it! She was sent alone as bait!

00:20:20.070 --> 00:20:22.520
Love Shower Pitch!

00:20:22.770 --> 00:20:25.020
NO!!!

00:20:25.170 --> 00:20:26.630
How about an encore?

00:20:26.780 --> 00:20:33.030
Wait a minute, you guys! {It's not}That wasn't an illusion, {but}it was a live concert!

00:20:33.090 --> 00:20:33.720
Hmph!

00:20:39.160 --> 00:20:39.820
Hanon?

00:20:40.330 --> 00:20:42.200
Huh? What happened to me?

00:20:42.580 --> 00:20:46.790
You {were so tired because you pedaled the}wore yourself out from pedaling your bike so hard{. You} and fell asleep during the illusion show.

00:20:47.200 --> 00:20:50.210
Really? That was so not cool of me.

00:20:50.290 --> 00:20:55.440
No, that's not the case. You were really brave, Nagisa.

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:56.160
Eh?

00:20:56.490 --> 00:20:59.650
I now understand my true feelings.

00:21:00.470 --> 00:21:02.330
Thank you, Nagisa.

00:21:03.810 --> 00:21:04.420
Hanon.

00:21:11.090 --> 00:21:12.850
The sky is filled with beautiful stars, Hanon.

00:21:13.230 --> 00:21:15.070
Yeah. They're beautiful.

00:21:17.160 --> 00:21:21.170
Tarou-chan, in your letter, you wrote,

00:21:21.680 --> 00:21:25.450
"Hanon-san, please find the person that you would treasure the most."

00:21:25.710 --> 00:21:28.470
"I'm sure that you would be able to find him."

00:21:28.980 --> 00:21:34.590
Tarou-chan, you were like a star in the sky that I could only gaze at.

00:21:34.850 --> 00:21:40.050
But now, I have someone who would look up at the sky with me.

00:21:40.490 --> 00:21:46.460
Tarou-chan, the person who I treasure most is beside me now.

00:21:47.170 --> 00:21:50.390
W-What's wrong, Hanon? Why aren't you looking at the stars?

00:21:50.640 --> 00:21:53.650
{That's because }I have something {more}else worth {seeing}looking at.

00:21:54.450 --> 00:21:55.210
What's that?

00:21:55.590 --> 00:21:57.990
{Goodness}Geez! Can you turn {more }towards me so that I can see it better?

00:23:51.310 --> 00:23:54.670
Kaito asked me to make a lunch for him!

00:23:54.900 --> 00:23:56.740
That's because he is going to practice surfing.

00:23:57.560 --> 00:24:00.110
Kaito's surely regained his heart!

00:24:00.720 --> 00:24:04.470
See! He's smiling at me.

00:24:05.290 --> 00:24:07.720
Kaito! Do your best!

00:24:08.280 --> 00:24:11.580
Next time on Mermaid Melody Pichi Pichi Pitch Pure:

00:24:11.860 --> 00:24:13.270
The Memory That Disappeared into the Sea.

00:24:13.930 --> 00:24:16.020
Wait, Kaito!

00:24:16.510 --> 00:24:19.400
Why did you choose not me, but Lucia-chan instead?
